    "title": "Fire forces garbage truck to dump load on Mandeville street - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Curt Sprang ,\n7 hours ago\nMANDEVILLE, La. ( WGNO ) ‚Äî A much-used stretch of road in Mandeville, the East Causeway Approach, was partially closed for more than two hours on Feb. 25 after a garbage truck dumped its load along the eastbound lanes.\nAccording to the Mandeville Police Department, the driver of the garbage truck noticed smoke coming from the back of it, and that‚Äôs when he pulled over and dumped the load in the street.\nPolice said that someone had discarded a lithium battery in the trash, and it ignited after garbage collection workers picked it up.\nScreenshot Screenshot Screenshot Firefighters quickly put out the flames but removing the garbage was a bigger job.\nMandeville police said the driver‚Äôs quick action prevented anyone from getting hurt and probably prevented the truck from going up in flames.\nMobile dog gym keeps Rover running on the Northshore Stay up to date with the latest news, weather and sports by downloading the WGNO app on the Apple or Google Play stores and by subscribing to the WGNO newsletter .\nLatest Posts Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WGNO.\n2",
    "summary": "( WGNO ) ‚Äî A much-used stretch of road in Mandeville, the East Causeway Approach, was partially closed for more than two hours on Feb. 25 after a garbage truck dumped its load along the eastbound lanes. According to the Mandeville Police Department, the driver of the garbage truck noticed smoke coming from the back of it, and that‚Äôs when he pulled over and dumped the load in the street. Police said that someone had discarded a lithium battery in the trash, and it ignited after garbage collection workers picked it up.",
